## What the defect actually was

src/commands_config.rs::handle_hooks printed a hand-written teaching block naming two phases (hooks.pre.bash, hooks.post.*) while HookPhase::ALL has held three since Day 202. The telling detail: hooks.rs's own doc comment promises "a phase added to the enum must be covered by this arm without an edit here" — and that held for every reader that goes through the enum (parser, unknown-phase warning, /hooks listing, trust refusal). The two teaching doors spell the vocabulary out as prose, so a new variant could not reach them by any mechanism. The drift wasn't a missed edit; it was the absence of a derivation.

## The fix (moved the statement to the authority, didn't add a third copy)

• **src/hooks.rs**: `HookPhase::usage_example()` and `HookPhase::what_it_does()` as exhaustive `match`es on `self` (a fourth variant is now E0004, not silence), plus `hook_phase_teaching_lines() which builds the block by iterating ALL, then the three shared closing sentences and a $TOOL_ERROR note. what_it_does` states the *facts* read off the wrapper's real `Ok`/`Err` seam (`Post` runs whether the tool succeeded or failed; `PostFailure` runs only on `Err` and can only add feedback).
• **src/commands_config.rs: the block is now a four-line loop; the file shrank** (1,999 lines against the 2,000 cap, and it is not register-exempt, so growing it wasn't an option).
• **tests/module_size.rs: pasted `("src/hooks.rs", 3545)` from what the gate printed**, after cargo fmt.
• **ARCHITECTURE.md**: Day 203 note appended to the `hooks.rs` entry; the call-site half recorded on the `commands_config_mcp.rs` entry (there is no separate bullet for its parent).

## Tests

Four in hooks.rs — derivation guard (reddens when a fourth phase is untaught), anti-vacuous (demo-line count == ALL.len(), since contains("") makes the first guard satisfiable by an empty block), the exact missing clause (post_failure + TOOL_ERROR), the shared-closing-facts near-miss — plus a cross-door guard asserting every usage_example() appears verbatim in help_data::command_help("hooks"). tests/integration.rs has one weak source-level guard at the emission point with its limit stated in the doc comment.

## Positive control — run serially as one atomic mutate→run→restore

Neutering PostFailure's usage_example arm reddened exactly 2 tests, both new (the derivation guard and the cross-door guard), no pre-existing test red, then restored to a clean tree with 0 markers. Note the red is wider than the task file's prediction of 1 — that's a fact about which tests read that line, so I'm stating 2 rather than massaging the control to match the plan.

cargo fmt --check, clippy --all-targets -D warnings, cargo build, and cargo test (17 suites, 5678 tests, 0 failures) all pass.

